1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,323
The Return With a Receipt.

3
00:00:03,323 --> 00:00:06,260
I buy a new notebook with tiny stars on the cover.

4
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:11,562
At home, I open it and discover that half the pages have the date and title boxes printed upside down.

5
00:00:11,562 --> 00:00:15,229
Unless I plan to write while standing on my head, something is wrong.

6
00:00:15,508 --> 00:00:17,470
Looks like a printing problem.

7
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:20,252
We can take it back and ask about an exchange.

8
00:00:20,524 --> 00:00:23,028
The next day, we return to the store.

9
00:00:23,028 --> 00:00:26,122
I keep the notebook and receipt together in a small bag.

10
00:00:26,122 --> 00:00:28,361
At the counter, I take a breath.

11
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:30,330
I'd like to exchange this.

12
00:00:30,604 --> 00:00:32,346
What's the problem with it?

13
00:00:32,572 --> 00:00:34,868
The pages are printed upside down.

14
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:38,024
I open the notebook and show her where the pattern changes.

15
00:00:38,308 --> 00:00:39,906
Oh, I see.

16
00:00:39,906 --> 00:00:41,520
Do you have the receipt?

17
00:00:41,788 --> 00:00:43,603
Yes, right here.

18
00:00:43,828 --> 00:00:44,988
Thanks.

19
00:00:44,988 --> 00:00:47,186
We can exchange it for another one.

20
00:00:47,186 --> 00:00:49,040
Would you like the same design?

21
00:00:49,324 --> 00:00:50,589
Definitely.

22
00:00:50,589 --> 00:00:52,557
I still like the stars.

23
00:00:52,557 --> 00:00:56,734
The clerk brings another notebook, and we check it together before I put it in my bag.

24
00:00:56,734 --> 00:00:59,078
All the pages look right this time.

25
00:00:59,356 --> 00:01:00,923
Nicely handled.

26
00:01:00,923 --> 00:01:03,204
You explained the problem clearly.

27
00:01:03,484 --> 00:01:05,632
I was worried I would sound rude.

28
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:08,479
Asking politely about a problem is okay.

29
00:01:08,479 --> 00:01:11,260
That's part of what the service desk is there for.

30
00:01:11,548 --> 00:01:14,406
At home, I write my name on the first page.

31
00:01:14,406 --> 00:01:17,865
The stars are still excellent, and my words are the right way up.

32
00:01:17,865 --> 00:01:19,804
Ben seems disappointed.

33
00:01:19,804 --> 00:01:22,823
He was looking forward to the upside-down writing experiment.
